{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}camelCase Table Names in MySQL on Windows{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">Dotkernel</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">camelCase Table Names in MySQL on Windows</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="container py-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
            
            {% include '@partial/left-menu.html.twig' %}

            <main class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-9">
                <article class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5 h-100">
                    <header class="mb-4">
                        <h1 class="h2 text-dark fw-bold">camelCase Table Names in MySQL on Windows</h1>
                        <div class="text-muted small">
                            <i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-1"></i> Dotkernel
                        </div>
                    </header>

                    <section class="post-content text-secondary lh-lg fs-6">
                        If you are using a WAMP stack, like WAMP or XAMPP, and try to create a table in camelCase ( example: <strong>adminLogin</strong>)  you will notice that camelCase is not working, table name will be lowercase: <strong>adminlogin</strong>.
In order to fix this, you need to add to your my.cnf file the line:
<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3 overflow-auto">>lower_case_table_names=2</pre>
and restart mysql.

More on that here: <a href="http://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/4.1/en/server-system-variables.html#sysvar_lower_case_table_names" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">http://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/4.1/en/server-system-variables.html#sysvar_lower_case_table_names</a>
                    </section>
                </article>
            </main>
            
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}